/-!
# Riemannian symmetric spaces

A Riemannian manifold `M` is a **Riemannian symmetric space** if every point `p : M` admits a
global **geodesic symmetry** `s_p ∈ Isom(M)`: an involutive smooth Riemannian self-isometry fixing
`p` whose differential at `p` is `-id` on `T_p M`.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.IsGeodesicSymmetryAt`: predicate asserting that a Riemannian self-isometry `Φ` is a
  geodesic symmetry at `p`.
* `TauCeti.IsRiemannianSymmetricSpace`: typeclass asserting that every point of `M` admits a global
  geodesic symmetry.
* `TauCeti.geodesicSymmetry`: a chosen geodesic symmetry `s_p ∈ Isom(M)` at `p` (unique on a
  preconnected manifold).
* `TauCeti.symmetrySubgroup`: the normal subgroup of `Isom(M)` generated by all geodesic
  symmetries.
* `TauCeti.transvectionSubgroup`: the normal subgroup of `Isom(M)` generated by products `s_p * s_q`
  of pairs of geodesic symmetries.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.isGeodesicSymmetryAt_of_mfderiv_eq_neg_id` and `TauCeti.IsGeodesicSymmetryAt.eq`: on a
  preconnected smooth Riemannian manifold, an isometry fixing `p` with differential `-id` is
  automatically involutive, and the geodesic symmetry at `p` is unique.
* `TauCeti.IsGeodesicSymmetryAt.exists_nhds_eq_of_apply_eq`: `p` is an isolated fixed point of any
  geodesic symmetry at `p`.
* `TauCeti.IsGeodesicSymmetryAt.apply_maximalGeodesic` and
  `TauCeti.IsGeodesicSymmetryAt.apply_riemannianExp`: a geodesic symmetry at `p` reverses geodesics
  through `p` (`s_p (γ(t)) = γ(-t)` and `s_p (exp_p v) = exp_p (-v)`).
* `TauCeti.IsGeodesicSymmetryAt.derivCurvatureTensor_eq_zero` and
  `TauCeti.hasParallelCurvature_leviCivitaConnection_of_isRiemannianSymmetricSpace`: every
  Riemannian symmetric space has parallel curvature (`∇R = 0`), hence is locally symmetric.
* `TauCeti.isGeodesicallyCompleteAt_of_isRiemannianSymmetricSpace`,
  `TauCeti.properSpace_of_isRiemannianSymmetricSpace`, and
  `TauCeti.completeSpace_of_isRiemannianSymmetricSpace`: every Riemannian symmetric space is
  geodesically complete, proper, and metrically complete.
* `TauCeti.isPretransitive_transvectionSubgroup` and
  `TauCeti.isPretransitive_isom_of_isRiemannianSymmetricSpace`: on a preconnected Riemannian
  symmetric space, the transvection group (hence the symmetry group and `Isom(M)`) acts
  transitively.
* `TauCeti.IsGeodesicSymmetryAt.mul_apply_isGeodesicCurve` and
  `TauCeti.IsGeodesicSymmetryAt.tangentMap_mul_of_alongCurve_eq_zero`: the transvection
  `s_{γ(b)} * s_{γ(a)}` translates an all-time geodesic `γ` by `2(b - a)` and realizes parallel
  transport along `γ`.
* `TauCeti.instIsRiemannianSymmetricSpaceProd`: a product of Riemannian symmetric spaces is a
  Riemannian symmetric space.

## References

* J.-H. Eschenburg, *Lecture Notes on Symmetric Spaces*, Augsburg, 1997, §§1–2.
* S. Helgason, *Differential Geometry, Lie Groups, and Symmetric Spaces*, Academic Press, 1978,
  Chapter IV, §§3–4.
* S. Kobayashi and K. Nomizu, *Foundations of Differential Geometry*, Vol. II, Interscience, 1969,
  Chapter XI, §3.
* J. M. Lee, *Introduction to Riemannian Manifolds*, 2nd ed., Springer GTM 176, 2018, Chapter 7.
-/

